dialect grammar
grammar stdio.docx.snapshot
extension xml
start document
comment none
string double raw
string single raw

# FG-wave (docx is this wave's OPC pattern-setter, see this ticket's own brief): `stdio.docx`
# (ECMA-376 WordprocessingML) is a ZIP/OPC package -- binary-native AT THE CONTAINER level (this
# facet's binary sibling, ../💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio, restates zip's own real ZIP/OPC
# byte layout, `🎒️zip/🏅️standards/🔖️2.0/…/📡️.protocol.semio`). THIS grammar facet
# instead models the real TEXT syntax of the XML parts an OPC docx package carries --
# `[Content_Types].xml`, `_rels/.rels` (+ any per-part `*.rels`), this format's own
# `word/document.xml` body, and `word/styles.xml` -- restated from xml's own real FG1 grammar
# (`📰xml/🏅️standards/🔖️1.0/🪆️subsets/✳️any/🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio`,
# cited verbatim wherever the shape is identical) since cross-artifact `use` does not resolve at
# walk time (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.1/§3) -- the SAME honest-restatement precedent every OPC
# family member has used since zip's own P2 pilot. This is the pattern the wave's sibling agents
# (xlsx, pptx, bcf, ifc/2x3) restate from in turn.
#
# Real element/attribute vocabulary traced directly from this artifact's own real Rust codec (not
# invented, not guessed):
# - `[Content_Types].xml`: `<Types xmlns=..>` / `<Default Extension=.. ContentType=../>` /
#   `<Override PartName=.. ContentType=../>` -- `🎒️zip/📦️opc/🦀️.rs`'s
#   `content_types_to_xml`/`content_types_from_xml` (:80-176, `CONTENT_TYPES_NS` :53).
# - `_rels/.rels` (and any per-part `*.rels`): `<Relationships xmlns=..>` /
#   `<Relationship Id=.. Type=.. Target=.. TargetMode=?../>` (`TargetMode` only present when
#   `External`) -- same file's `relationships_to_xml`/`relationships_from_xml` (:178-292,
#   `RELATIONSHIPS_NS` :54).
# - `word/document.xml`: `<w:document xmlns:w=..><w:body>(w:p|w:tbl)*</w:body></w:document>`, each
#   `w:p` a `w:pPr?` (`w:pStyle w:val=`, then raw-retained extension content) + `w:r`*
#   (`w:rPr?`(`w:b`/`w:i`/`w:u w:val="single"`, then raw-retained extension content) +
#   `w:t xml:space="preserve"`text), each `w:tbl` a `w:tblPr?`(raw-retained) + `w:tr`*
#   (`w:trPr?`(raw-retained) + `w:tc`*(`w:tcPr?`(raw-retained) + nested `(w:p|w:tbl)*`)) --
#   `⚙️engine/🦀️.rs`'s `document_to_xml`/`document_from_xml`/`paragraph_to_xml`/
#   `run_to_xml`/`table_to_xml`/`row_to_xml`/`cell_to_xml` (:63-288). "Raw-retained extension
#   content" = this artifact's own `extra_*_properties: Vec<XmlNode>` fields (any `w:rPr`/`w:pPr`/
#   `w:trPr`/`w:tcPr`/`w:tblPr` child this typed model doesn't interpret, carried verbatim on
#   round-trip, per `📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s own doc comment) -- modeled below as `x-elem*`,
#   a restatement of xml's own generic recursive element/content grammar (`x-` prefixed to avoid
#   colliding with this file's own docx-specific production names).
# - `word/styles.xml`: `<w:styles xmlns:w=..>(<w:style w:styleId=><w:name w:val=/>
#   <w:basedOn w:val=/>?</w:style>)*</w:styles>` -- same engine file's `styles_to_xml`/
#   `styles_from_xml` (:293-338).
#
# `comment none`: XML has no `#`-comment syntax (same rationale xml's own grammar file documents --
# this vocabulary's numeric character references, if any future growth needed them, use `#` as a
# literal sigil immediately after `&`).
#
# `string double raw` + `string single raw` (restated verbatim from xml's own grammar, same real
# quirk): every attribute value here is quoted `"`/`'` and captured VERBATIM -- entity decoding in
# this artifact's own real parser only ever runs over element CONTENT text (`xml_unescape_text`,
# transitively via the shared `xml_document_from_text`), never attribute values.
#
# `<`/`>`/`&`/`;` below are the P2-M1-promoted single-char terminals (LT/GT/AMP/SEMICOLON); `:`
# (namespace-prefixed names, `w:document`/`xml:space`/…) was already a real single-char lexer
# token, so a colon-bearing name is modeled the SAME way xml's own `name = IDENT ":" IDENT | IDENT`
# production does -- decomposed into separate literal tokens, never one fused literal string.
document = part+
part = content-types-part | relationships-part | document-part | styles-part

# ── [Content_Types].xml ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
content-types-part = LT "Types" "xmlns" "=" TEXT GT ct-entry* LT "/" "Types" GT
ct-entry = ct-default | ct-override
ct-default = LT "Default" "Extension" "=" TEXT "ContentType" "=" TEXT "/" GT
ct-override = LT "Override" "PartName" "=" TEXT "ContentType" "=" TEXT "/" GT

# ── _rels/.rels (and any per-part *.rels) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
relationships-part = LT "Relationships" "xmlns" "=" TEXT GT relationship* LT "/" "Relationships" GT
relationship = LT "Relationship" "Id" "=" TEXT "Type" "=" TEXT "Target" "=" TEXT rel-target-mode? "/" GT
rel-target-mode = "TargetMode" "=" TEXT

# ── word/document.xml ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
document-part = LT "w" ":" "document" "xmlns" ":" "w" "=" TEXT GT LT "w" ":" "body" GT block* LT "/" "w" ":" "body" GT LT "/" "w" ":" "document" GT
block = paragraph | table

paragraph = LT "w" ":" "p" GT para-props? run* LT "/" "w" ":" "p" GT
para-props = LT "w" ":" "pPr" GT para-style? x-elem* LT "/" "w" ":" "pPr" GT
para-style = LT "w" ":" "pStyle" "w" ":" "val" "=" TEXT "/" GT

run = LT "w" ":" "r" GT run-props? run-text LT "/" "w" ":" "r" GT
run-props = LT "w" ":" "rPr" GT run-flag* x-elem* LT "/" "w" ":" "rPr" GT
# `w:b`/`w:i` are UNATTRIBUTED self-closing tags (`<w:b/>`, no space, no attribute between the
# name and `/`) -- confirmed live (a real conformance-test bisection, not assumed) that the shared
# lexer's `is_ident_continue` includes `/` (`🔍️lexer/🦀️.rs`'s own `is_ident_continue`,
# alongside `_`/`-`/`.`) -- so with NOTHING between the element name and the slash, the two fuse
# into ONE `IDENT` token (`"b/"`, not `"b"` then `"/"`); `w:pStyle`'s own self-closing tag never
# hits this because its attribute's closing quote breaks the identifier run before `/`. Modeled as
# ONE fused-literal token below (`"b/"`/`"i/"`), not two separate tokens -- this is a genuine,
# artifact-agnostic lexer property (any unattributed self-closing tag immediately followed by `/`
# hits it), not a docx-specific hack; `w:u` never needs this treatment since it always carries
# `w:val=`.
run-flag = bold-flag | italic-flag | underline-flag
bold-flag = LT "w" ":" "b/" GT
italic-flag = LT "w" ":" "i/" GT
underline-flag = LT "w" ":" "u" "w" ":" "val" "=" TEXT "/" GT
run-text = LT "w" ":" "t" "xml" ":" "space" "=" TEXT GT text-run? LT "/" "w" ":" "t" GT
text-run = {IDENT | INT | FLOAT}+

table = LT "w" ":" "tbl" GT table-props? row* LT "/" "w" ":" "tbl" GT
table-props = LT "w" ":" "tblPr" GT x-elem* LT "/" "w" ":" "tblPr" GT
row = LT "w" ":" "tr" GT row-props? cell* LT "/" "w" ":" "tr" GT
row-props = LT "w" ":" "trPr" GT x-elem* LT "/" "w" ":" "trPr" GT
cell = LT "w" ":" "tc" GT cell-props? block* LT "/" "w" ":" "tc" GT
cell-props = LT "w" ":" "tcPr" GT x-elem* LT "/" "w" ":" "tcPr" GT

# ── word/styles.xml ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
styles-part = LT "w" ":" "styles" "xmlns" ":" "w" "=" TEXT GT style* LT "/" "w" ":" "styles" GT
style = LT "w" ":" "style" "w" ":" "styleId" "=" TEXT GT LT "w" ":" "name" "w" ":" "val" "=" TEXT "/" GT style-based-on? LT "/" "w" ":" "style" GT
style-based-on = LT "w" ":" "basedOn" "w" ":" "val" "=" TEXT "/" GT

# ── Raw-retained extension content (`extra_*_properties: Vec<XmlNode>`) ──────────────────────────
# Restated (not `use`d) from xml's own generic recursive element/content grammar -- the SAME
# `📰xml/…/📸️snapshot/📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio` productions this file cites above,
# `x-`-prefixed to stay a distinct namespace from this file's own docx-specific productions. Covers
# any future/unmodeled `w:rPr`/`w:pPr`/`w:trPr`/`w:tcPr`/`w:tblPr` child this typed model doesn't
# interpret but must still round-trip verbatim.
x-elem = x-empty-tag | x-open-tag x-content x-close-tag
x-empty-tag = LT x-name x-attr* "/" GT
x-open-tag = LT x-name x-attr* GT
x-close-tag = LT "/" x-name GT
x-attr = x-name "=" TEXT
x-name = IDENT ":" IDENT | IDENT
x-content = {x-elem | x-reference | x-cdata | x-comment | text-run}*
x-reference = x-entity-ref | x-char-ref
x-entity-ref = AMP IDENT SEMICOLON
x-char-ref = AMP "#" INT SEMICOLON | AMP "#" IDENT SEMICOLON
x-cdata = LT "!" "[" "CDATA" "[" x-cdata-body "]" "]" GT
x-cdata-body = {IDENT | INT | FLOAT}*
x-comment = LT "!" "--" x-comment-body "--" GT
x-comment-body = {IDENT | INT | FLOAT}*
